Setup
=====

Prepare this configuration for your installed NixOS system, then build and apply
it.

Use the installed target system and its existing normal account. Preserve the actual
hardware module, boot disk settings and system.stateVersion baseline. Never substitute
another machine's filesystem identifiers.

Review hosts/desktop/settings.nix and the supplied modules. Prepare a new writable
checkout using bash scripts/prepare.sh; use --help for required hardware, boot
mode and compatibility-baseline arguments. The baseline must match the installed
system. Preparation locks dependencies without activation. Then use the
check/build/apply commands below from that working checkout.

From a prepared working checkout:

   nix --extra-experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' flake check --no-write-lock-file
   nix --extra-experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' build --no-write-lock-file --no-link .#nixosConfigurations.desktop.config.system.build.toplevel
   sudo nixos-rebuild switch --option experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' --no-write-lock-file --flake .#desktop

After applying, verify your account and administrative access before rebooting. Keep
the current terminal open until a new login succeeds.
